+### Transferring a user to another organization
+
+`POST /orgs/{orgID}/users/{uid}/transfer` with `{"toOrgId":"globex"}` moves a
+user from `{orgID}` to another organization (for example between group companies).
+
+- Only org admins of `{orgID}` may transfer its users. Another organization's
+  path → 404; a same-org user who is not an org admin → 403.
+- The user must belong to `{orgID}`; otherwise 404.
+- `toOrgId` must differ from `{orgID}` (400) and must be an existing organization (400).
+  There is no organizations table: an organization exists when at least one user belongs to it.
+- The transfer is all or nothing, and it keeps the model rules:
+  - the user's memberships in projects of the old organization are removed;
+  - tasks assigned to the user in those projects are unassigned, including in archived projects
+    (a transfer is an organization operation, not a write to the project);
+  - the user's org admin flag is cleared, since admin rights belong to the organization.
+- The user gets no memberships in the new organization.
+
